                <pb facs="0723" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg709"/>

                <head><seg type="margin">[701]</seg> *<hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Preston, Secretary
                        of the Navy, to Commander Randolph, United States Navy.</hi></head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department</hi></placeName>,
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1849-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >September</hi> 20, 1849</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The official reports of your proceedings
                    and movements with a portion of the home squadron under your command, in the
                    neighborhood of Round Island, dated 25th and 28th of August, and 1st and 5th of
                    September, 1849, and the inclosures relating thereto, have been received.</p>
                <p>The prompt, the decisive, and the satisfactory manner in which you have executed
                    the confidential instructions of the 9th ultimo, addressed to Commodore Foxhall
                    A. Parker, is fully approved by the Department.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>WM. BALLARD PRESTON.</item>
                            <item>Commander <hi rendition="#small-caps">Victor M.
                                    Randolph</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Commanding U. S. Ship
                                    Albany, off Pascagoula, Mississippi.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
